<title>ITALY: Italy budget health savings worth 1.5trln lire-Min.</title>
<headline>Italy budget health savings worth 1.5trln lire-Min.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1997 budget will seek savings of 1.5 trillion lire from the health service, Health Minister Rosi Bindi told reporters as she left a cabinet meeting which was called to approve the budget package.</p>
<p>She said the meeting was continuing.</p>
<p>Government sources said earlier on Friday the whole budget package would slash 62.5 trillion lire off next year's deficit. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
